## Antigravity specifics

- **Skills and agents** — the rolepod skills ship inside the plugin
  (`~/.gemini/config/plugins/rolepod/skills/`) and show as slash commands
  (e.g. `/write-spec`); 15 specialists ship as plugin subagents, each
  carrying its own protocol. agy does not dispatch by description: spawn
  the specialist a skill names, by its name.
- **Tier classes** — cheap / balanced / strong are CLASSES, never model
  names; agy picks models, so request by class: sweep / read = the fast
  class, build / verify = the pro class, strong = the strongest available;
  cannot classify → balanced, and say so.
- **workflow.mode** — Lite / Standard / Full never change which gates hold. The private-docs deny runs on every CLI and the sub-agent commit ban on Codex and opencode; review / test evidence, cannot-wait, sibling-edit and fan-out gates are Claude-only. Nothing else is mechanically enforced here — never report it as such. agy has no context-injection channel, so this file is the only always-on text.
